Kylene is a Statistics and Data Science major with a Minor in Mathematics at UTSA. 
Her research interests primarily focus on mathematical models and how they can be 
applied to biological systems. Within the Camacho Lab, she assists with wet lab 
experiments such as cryosectioning and ERGs, as well as dry lab work. In the 
future, she wishes to pursue her PhD in Computational Biology. Outside of the 
lab, she loves botany and painting. 
